Probability of drawing a white ball given Bag B was selected: \(P(E/E_2) = \frac{3}{3+2} = \frac{3}{5}\)
We need to find the probability that the ball was drawn from Bag A, given that the ball drawn is white, i.e., \(P(E_1/E)\). Using Bayes' Theorem:
P(E_1/E) = \frac{P(E_1)P(E/E_1)}{P(E_1)P(E/E_1) + P(E_2)P(E/E_2)}
= \frac{\frac{1}{2} \times \frac{3}{10}}{\frac{1}{2} \times \frac{3}{10} + \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{3}{5}}
= \frac{\frac{3}{20}}{\frac{3}{20} + \frac{6}{20}}
= \frac{\frac{3}{20}}{\frac{9}{20}}
= \frac{3}{9} = \frac{1}{3}

